# Shared build-context ignore for BOTH images (docker/Dockerfile and
# docker/dev.Dockerfile). BuildKit applies the context-root .dockerignore to a
# build whose Dockerfile has no adjacent <name>.dockerignore — and it does NOT
# merge a root file with a per-Dockerfile one (the per-file one fully replaces
# the root). So a single root file here is what lets both builds share these
# globs without duplication.
#
# tests/ is intentionally NOT excluded: the dev image COPYs it in, while the
# runtime image stays lean by only COPYing pyproject.toml + src (never tests/) —
# so the image leanness comes from the Dockerfile's COPY list, not from ignoring
# tests here.
.git
.github
.idea
.vscode
.pytest_cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
# Never send tokens or scraped output into a build. Env files are loaded by
# compose at runtime (env_file:), never COPYed into an image, so exclude them all.
.env*
output/
.venv/
venv/
# Not needed to build or run either image.
docs/
docker/
